Drop the nose setup_requires from mockredispy's sdist.

nose was abandoned upstream and has no release that imports on Python 3.10+
(it still uses `collections.Callable`). mockredispy only lists it so that
`python setup.py nosetests` works and so it can register a nose plugin
entry point -- neither matters when all we want is the built wheel, and the
mock_tables shims that consume this package import mockredis directly.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -13,9 +13,6 @@
       license='Apache2',
       packages=find_packages(exclude=['*.tests']),
-      setup_requires=[
-          'nose'
-      ],
       extras_require={
           'lua': ['lunatic-python-bugfix==1.1.1'],
       },
